{
  "case_id": "CASE-007",
  "category": "vrptw_lns_ejection",
  "description": [
    "Problem and initialization: Read a Solomon-style time-window routing instance and build an initial solution with the greedy heuristic. The entry point requests 100 customers.\n\n",
    "Combination: First run a fleet-reduction phase that removes and reinserts customers and may invoke ejection search for unserved requests. Then apply a randomly selected destroy neighborhood and a repairer to a candidate, keep the best solution, and use the implementation's acceptance and larger-removal controls. In the main phase, the repair selector returns random-order insertion for draws below 10 and regret-2 otherwise; its nested branch for other choices is unreachable.\n\n",
    "Boundary: The fleet-reduction loop counts 200000 iterations and the main loop counts 500000 nonempty destroy iterations. The main counter is decremented when a destroy operation removes nothing, so total attempts are not bounded by that counter. It requires a compatible input instance and a C++ environment. The deviation variable can be read without being initialized when an infeasible or too-many-routes trial is rejected before the variable is assigned; it may also contain a stale value. The syntax check does not establish constraint correctness or solution quality."
  ],
